//! The non-generic runtime functions take exactly the parameter types lowering declares at their call sites.
//!
//! Lowering calls each of them as a native external with those types (question Q1). The driver refuses a plan whose
//! declared signature differs from the compiled function's ("external metadata differs from the admitted safe scalar
//! signature"), so each function is pinned here as a function-pointer coercion. Generated by
//! `run1/tools/call_site_signatures.rb` from the reference frames, with the call sites that pass owned values where the
//! reference frame borrowed taken from lowering (`run1/audit/runtime-call-sites.txt`).

